      "synthesis": {
        "main_text_has_explicit_synthesis": true,
        "si_used": false,
        "procedure": "A methanol solution (1 mL) of DyCl3·6H2O (0.05 mmol, 0.0185 g), CoCl2·6H2O (0.05 mmol, 0.0119 g), H2L1 (0.1 mmol, 0.0186 g), and an acetonitrile solution (1 mL) of HL2 (0.05 mmol, 0.0107 g) were mixed and added into an 18 cm-long Pyrex tube with one end closed. After addition of trimethylamine (0.25 mmol, 35 μL), the tube was sealed under vacuum and heated in an oven at 90 °C for 1 day, then slowly cooled to room temperature, giving red crystals.",
